. I also know why the books keep getting pushed to \"later.\" Chair and Ledger exists so the books stop waiting.\n\nI work only with salons. Every client I have is a hair or nail salon, so I'm not learning your business at your expense.\n\n## What you get for $199 a month\n\n- **Monthly books**, closed by the 10th of the following month\n- **Payroll** for up to 10 staff\n- **Sales tax filing**\n\nYou pay one flat monthly fee, and payroll is part of it, not an add-on.\n\n## Closed by the 10th, or that month is free\n\nEach month's books are closed by the 10th of the next month. If I miss that date, you don't pay for that month.\n\n## Clean books show up at tax time\n\nLast tax season, nine of my clients told me their accountant charged them less because their books came in clean. One of them saved $800.\n\nI can't promise what your accountant will charge. I can promise that the books they get from me will be complete, organized, and on time.\n\n## Salons stay\n\nI work with 31 salons right now. Two clients left last year, and both left because they sold their salons.\n\n## Who you'll be working with\n\nYou'll work with me. Chair and Ledger is one person, so you won't be handed off to someone new who has to learn your salon from scratch. It also means I don't take calls on Sundays or Mondays. Those are my days off, and the rest of the week is for my clients.\n\n## Start with a free 20-minute call\n\nThe first call is free and takes 20 minutes. We'll talk about your salon and whether I'm the right fit. Calls run Tuesday through Saturday, so pick a time that works around your appointments.\n\n**[Book your free 20-minute call]**\n</final_document>\n\nA few notes:\n- It's about 340 words.\n- **Left out:** the three missed deadlines, the old $149 price, and which states you cover. You can add the states later if you want to.\n- **The guarantee:** I wrote it as \"that month is free.\" That covers the month whose books came in late, not the month you missed the deadline in. 